  "comment": "The SRTM was flown on an 11-day mission of the Space Shuttle Endeavour in February of 2000. The Shuttle Radar Topography Mission ( SRTM ) is an international research effort that obtained digital elevation models on a near-global scale from 56° S to 60° N, to generate the most complete high-resolution digital topographic database of Earth prior to the release of the ASTER GDEM in 2009. SRTM",
